  "view": "Gold fell about 1.3% to near $4,110 as Fed minutes kept a December hike on the table and the 10-year Treasury yield held near 5.3%. Soft September payrolls (+29,000) cut October hike odds to roughly 20%, but that has not been enough to lift bullion. Central bank buying, led by China's 21 tonnes in September, offers a floor but no near-term catalyst. Flow is bearish.",
