      "essay": "Shiksha, the education platform, billed ₹20.5 crore in Q2FY27, down 27.2% from ₹28.1 crore a year earlier. H1 billings fell 24.5% to ₹55.1 crore from ₹72.9 crore.\n\nInfo Edge tied the decline to AI-driven search engines answering user queries directly, which cuts the referral traffic Shiksha used to get from search results. The company is changing the platform's business model and adding new offerings to lower its dependence on search queries, but it expects billings growth to stay under pressure in the interim, with the transition playing out over the medium term. Shiksha is small next to recruitment, so the damage to group billings is limited. The read-through matters more: it shows what AI search can do to a lead-generation business, and the answer so far is a decline the company has no quick fix for.",
