      "headline": "Info Edge Q2 billings up 12.8%, Shiksha drags",
      "essay": "Info Edge reported standalone billings of ₹822.3 crore for Q2 FY27, up 12.8% from ₹729 crore a year earlier. The recruitment segment, which runs Naukri, rose 12.6% to ₹613.8 crore. The 99acres real-estate platform grew 21.2% to ₹148.3 crore. Shiksha, the education search vertical, fell 27.2% to ₹20.5 crore amid AI-driven competition for search traffic.\n\nFor H1 FY27, total standalone billings grew 13.5% to ₹1,559.3 crore from ₹1,373.2 crore. The stock slipped 3% after the update as investors weighed the Shiksha decline against the headline growth.\n\nThe mix matters for anyone holding the stock. Naukri and 99acres are carrying the company, while Shiksha shows how quickly a search-dependent vertical can erode when generative AI changes how people find information.",
      "sources": [1, 3, 4]
