    {
      "headline": "Brokerages stay bullish, 20 of 22 rate buy",
      "essay": "After the Q2 update, 20 of the 22 analysts covering Info Edge have a buy rating, with two holds. JPMorgan is overweight with a ₹1,500 target, Citi is buy at ₹1,510, and Nomura is buy at ₹1,480. Kotak Institutional Equities also upgraded the stock to buy.\n\nJPMorgan said Naukri's growth adjusted for client timing delays was 14% to 15%, in line with Q1's adjusted 15%. It attributed the growth to premiumization, with newer offerings like AI-Rex and Talent Pulse taking a larger share of new client additions alongside price increases. Citi noted that recruitment billings can swing quarter to quarter because some customers renew early and others defer.\n\nThe consensus view is that the underlying recruitment business is steadier than the reported 12.6% suggests, and that 99acres beat expectations.",
      "sources": [2, 5, 6]
    },
